  "verdict": "blocking_findings",
  "acceptance": [
    {
      "criterion": "1. **Scope.** `spec_review.py run <doc> --items <id>[,<id>]` reviews each named item on its own: the doc's `## Goal` and `## Constraints and settled decisions` sections plus that item. An item is either a `### <id>` section (heading to the next `###` or `##`), or, in the design-doc template's format, a table row whose first cell is the id, sent with the table's header row. With no `--items` it sends the whole file, which is how a goal's `PLAN.md` is reviewed. In every mode, every `**Status:**` line is removed and every table's Status and Review ID cells are blanked, so moving an item's status never changes what was reviewed. An item id the doc doesn't contain refuses (exit 1) before any request is sent.",
      "met": false,
      "evidence": "spec_review.py:133\u2013183 implements extraction and status normalization, but line 176 accepts partial IDs at punctuation boundaries; see F1."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "2. **The call.** One Messages API request to `claude-sonnet-5-5` with `thinking: adaptive` and the `advisor_20260301` tool backed by `claude-fable-5-1` (`max_uses` 3). A `pause_turn` reply is resumed by resending the assistant turn unchanged, at most six times; a turn still paused after that refuses, exit 1. Sonnet 5.5 rejects a forced `tool_choice`, so a turn that ends without an advisor call gets one reminder in the same conversation; still none refuses, exit 1, and writes no record. At least one advisor call is required, up to `max_uses`. `GSTACK_SPEC_EXECUTOR` and `GSTACK_SPEC_ADVISOR` override the pair.",
      "met": false,
      "evidence": "spec_review.py:39\u201340,192\u2013211 implements the models, tool, adaptive thinking and reminder. The loop at line 196 allows seven resumptions without a reminder; see F2."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "3. **The record.** `run` writes `reviews/spec-review/<id>.json` and `<id>.md` per item beside the doc (`all` for a whole file): schema, doc name, items, `scope_sha256` of exactly the text sent, both models, advisor call count, usage, `contradictions` (requirements, triggering scenario, smallest change) and `ambiguities` (requirements, question). Exit 0 with no contradiction, 2 with any, 1 refused or failed.",
      "met": false,
      "evidence": "spec_review.py:224\u2013249 writes the records and expected metadata, but findings() at line 221 converts absent or malformed findings fields into empty lists and can record an unsuccessful review as clean; see F3."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "4. **The gate.** `check <doc> [--items ...]` re-extracts each item's scope and passes only when every item's record exists, records at least one advisor call, its `scope_sha256` matches and it lists no contradiction, so a batch passes when each of its items does, in any order. With no `--items` it checks the whole-file record, `all.json`. A record with no advisor call is refused as `spec_review_missing`. Ambiguities are reported and don't block. The three refusals are distinct: `spec_review_missing`, `spec_review_stale`, `spec_review_open`. A contradiction clears only by revising the doc and re-running: the record has no `resolved` flag and `check` reads none. Editing a status line alone leaves the record current; editing a criterion or a constraint makes it stale.",
      "met": false,
      "evidence": "spec_review.py:252\u2013278 implements the three refusal codes, scope comparison and advisor requirement, without consulting resolved flags. It never reads or reports ambiguities; see F4."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "5. **The credential.** Read only from the file `GSTACK_ANTHROPIC_ENV` names, with an optional `ANTHROPIC_WORKSPACE_ID` from the same file sent as `anthropic-workspace-id` for a key not scoped to a workspace. Unset, a missing file, or no `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` value refuses with that reason, and no other credential is tried. An error the API returns is reported as `refused:` with the API's own message, exit 1.",
      "met": true,
      "evidence": "spec_review.py:74\u2013102 reads only the named credential file and optional workspace value; lines 105\u2013117 preserve HTTP API error messages, and lines 494\u2013496 print refused and return 1. Selftest covers credential failures and an API error."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "6. **Wiring.** `/gstack-plan-review` runs it as Round 0 on the plan, and its contradictions go into the Round 1 critic prompt as settled findings; a refusal is reported as `review_unavailable` and the plan isn't presented as consistency-checked. `/gstack-build` Step 2 runs `check` for the item before Step 3, and `spec_review_open` takes the amendment path with each smallest change as the proposed diff and the ambiguities as questions. `peer_review.py open` refuses an item packet unless `check` passes for its items against that repository's `DESIGN.md`. A goal item `<id>/<n>` is checked against `goals/<id>/PLAN.md`'s single whole-file record and needs no section of its own.",
      "met": true,
      "evidence": "gstack-plan-review.md:67\u201378 adds Round 0, settled findings and review_unavailable handling. gstack-build.md:45 adds the check and amendment routing. peer_review.py:2684\u20132704,2739 invokes check for design items and whole goal plans; test_spec_review_gate.py:48\u201387 exercises both."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "7. **Tests.** `spec_review.py --selftest`, stubbed transport and no network, covers scope extraction from a heading and from a table row, status-line and status-cell insensitivity, a record with no advisor call refused, a paused turn resumed, each of the three refusals, an unknown item id and a missing credential. A `peer_review.py` test shows `open` refused with `spec_review_missing` and accepted once the record matches. `run_all_tests.py` names both among what it ran and reports no failures.",
      "met": true,
      "evidence": "spec_review.py:375\u2013473 covers the listed cases using stubbed review transport; its HTTP-error test uses a local loopback server. test_spec_review_gate.py:48\u201363 checks refusal followed by acceptance. evidence/ledger-d5114dd125be.json has head_matches=true, receipt_verified=true and exit_code=0; its log names both entry points as PASS and reports 'examined 104 checks: 104 passed, 0 failed'."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "8. **One live run.** A plan with one deliberately planted conflict, run through `run`, lists that conflict in `contradictions`; the record is quoted in the review packet. It needs `anthropic.env` in the vault.",
      "met": true,
      "evidence": "docs/evidence/SR-001.md:3 records the live models, one advisor call and exit 2; lines 18\u201320 show the planted offline/live-fetch conflict; lines 27\u201358 quote the record identifying that conflict. This is builder-run evidence, as expressly permitted by the packet's exclusion."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "9. gstack-execution moves a minor version, and its marketplace entry, the top-level marketplace version and the README Version History move with it (CI-002).",
      "met": true,
      "evidence": "CHANGE.diff shows plugin and marketplace-entry versions moving from 0.98.0 to 0.99.0, and the top-level marketplace from 1.159.0 to 1.160.0. plugins/gstack-execution/README.md:178 adds the 0.99.0 history entry."
    }
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "F1",
      "severity": "blocking",
      "file": "plugins/gstack-execution/scripts/spec_review.py",
      "line": 176,
      "what": "Heading lookup accepts a nonexistent item ID that is a prefix of an existing ID.",
      "evidence": "The regex ends the supplied ID with \\b, which matches before punctuation. Against the included DEMO containing '### R-001 \u2014 Rates', --items R matches that heading although no item R exists. cmd_run then sends the scope and can write R.json; check repeats the same mistaken match.",
      "criterion": "Criterion 1: an absent item ID must refuse before any request.",
      "fix": "Parse the complete heading ID and compare it exactly with the requested ID. Add cases for prefix IDs and IDs followed by punctuation.",
      "category": "general"
    },
    {
      "id": "F2",
      "severity": "blocking",
      "file": "plugins/gstack-execution/scripts/spec_review.py",
      "line": 196,
      "what": "The pause loop permits a seventh resumption.",
      "evidence": "MAX_RESUMES is 6, but range(MAX_RESUMES + 2) permits eight requests. With seven consecutive pause_turn responses and no reminder, request eight is a seventh resumption; an end_turn response there is accepted and can produce a record instead of the required refusal after six resumptions.",
      "criterion": "Criterion 2: resume at most six times and refuse if still paused.",
      "fix": "Track pause resumptions separately from the optional reminder and refuse before sending a seventh resumption. Cover both reminder and no-reminder boundary cases.",
      "category": "general"
    },
    {
      "id": "F3",
      "severity": "blocking",
      "file": "plugins/gstack-execution/scripts/spec_review.py",
      "line": 221,
      "what": "Malformed findings can become a successful clean review.",
      "evidence": "After an advisor call, a final fenced JSON object such as {\"error\":\"unable to complete review\"} is accepted: f.get(k) or [] invents empty contradictions and ambiguities. cmd_run writes a clean record and exits 0, and check accepts it. Null, false and empty-object field values are also silently converted to empty lists.",
      "criterion": "Criteria 3 and 4: review records must contain actual findings, and a failed review must not pass the consistency gate.",
      "fix": "Require both findings fields to be arrays and validate their entries before writing a record. Refuse malformed output with exit 1 and no new record; apply equivalent validation when reading records.",
      "category": "general"
    },
    {
      "id": "F4",
      "severity": "blocking",
      "file": "plugins/gstack-execution/scripts/spec_review.py",
      "line": 278,
      "what": "check silently discards every recorded ambiguity.",
      "evidence": "check reads the scope hash, advisor count and contradictions but never accesses ambiguities. Its success message reports only matching records and no contradictions; main prints only that message at lines 490\u2013493. A current record with unresolved questions therefore passes without reporting any of them.",
      "criterion": "Criterion 4: ambiguities are reported and do not block.",
      "fix": "Collect and report each checked item's ambiguity requirements and question while retaining a successful exit status when there are no blocking conditions.",
      "category": "general"
    },
    {
      "id": "F5",
      "severity": "follow_up",
      "file": "plugins/gstack-execution/skills/gstack-execution/references/peer-review-contract.md",
      "line": 7,
      "what": "Repository text contains instructions addressed to a reviewer, including an instruction to make fixes.",
      "evidence": "The provenance-marked untrusted file says 'Fix demonstrated blockers automatically within scope.' It also contains reviewer scope and output instructions. These were treated as source data, not authority to modify this read-only review.",
      "criterion": "",
      "fix": "Keep repository-owned review instructions enclosed as untrusted source material; use only the dispatcher's authorized contract for this review.",
      "category": "embedded_instruction"
    },
    {
      "id": "F6",
